      "rev_n_1_1fd511_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_1fd511_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_1fd511",
        "thought_text": "The current dynamic programming approach is inefficient for large N and K values due to its O(N^2 * K) time complexity. We can optimize this by using a more efficient method, such as matrix exponentiation or a sliding window approach, which can reduce the time complexity to O(log N * K).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_1fd511_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_e9a72b51a4",
        "created_at": 1794531406.3462155
      },
      "rev_n_2_ce1864_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_ce1864_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_ce1864",
        "thought_text": "Mathematical formula derivation is not the most efficient approach for this problem, especially given the large constraints. A more effective approach would be to use dynamic programming with space optimization, as the current implementation is causing a time limit exceeded error due to its O(N^2 * K) time complexity.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_ce1864_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_7161ec9079",
        "created_at": 1794531441.0464556
      },
      "rev_n_3_0f7549_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_0f7549_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_0f7549",
        "thought_text": "The current approach is inefficient due to its O(N^2 * K) time complexity, which is too slow for large inputs. We can optimize this by using a prefix sum array to reduce the time complexity to O(N * K).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
