        "node_id": "n_4_e7e545",
        "thought_text": "The current approach using matrix exponentiation is correct in principle, but it's inefficient for large N values. Consider using a sliding window approach with a segment tree or Fenwick tree to reduce the time complexity to O(N log N), which should be sufficient for the given constraints.",
